description:
pkix-chain-simple/src/lib.rs:403

  policy.max_path_len = MAX_INTERMEDIATES as u8;

MAX_INTERMEDIATES is a usize constant (value 2). The cast to u8 will silently truncate if MAX_INTERMEDIATES is ever changed to a value >= 256. Clippy pedantic flags this as 'casting usize to u8 may truncate the value'.

The fix is to use u8::try_from(MAX_INTERMEDIATES).expect("MAX_INTERMEDIATES must fit in u8") or to declare MAX_INTERMEDIATES as u8 directly (currently it must be usize to be used in .len() comparisons, but the ValidationPolicy field is u8).

Simplest fix: add a compile-time assertion or change the type.
  const MAX_INTERMEDIATES: usize = 2;
  const _: () = assert!(MAX_INTERMEDIATES <= u8::MAX as usize);

Then replace the cast with u8::try_from(MAX_INTERMEDIATES).expect("constant fits in u8").
